children.doc:
Control engineering for any dynamic model: linear analysis, actuators and loop architecture, closed-loop
simulation, tuning and robustness (simulation only, no path to real equipment).

* :mod:`.analysis`: trim, linearisation, stability (growth rates, doubling times), controllability / observability,
  transfer functions, gain / phase / delay margins and peak sensitivity, step-response metrics.
* :mod:`.loop`:
  - :class:`Plant`, and :class:`Actuator` (range, rate limit, lag, dead band, delay, integrating);
  - controllers: :class:`PID` (derivative on measurement or rate, filter, back-calculation anti-windup,
    setpoint weighting, feed-forward), :class:`Cascade`, :class:`StateFeedback`;
  - :func:`simulate_loop`, :func:`loop_eigenvalues` (the complete discrete closed loop around an equilibrium)
    and :func:`compare_architectures` (which variable the controller commands).
* :mod:`.tuning`:
  - FOPDT fit, SIMC, IMC, Ziegler-Nichols;
  - PID pole placement for second-order plants, stable or not;
  - LQR;
  - tuning by optimisation under constraints, and Monte Carlo robustness.

Domain plants built on it: :mod:`pinneapple_simulation.naval` (submarine depth-keeping, ship roll stability).

functions.doc:
Return a callable that honours the contract, wrapping ``model`` when it does not.

* already takes ``theta`` (arity 2) → used as is, output normalised;
* takes only ``X`` (arity 1) and ``n_latent == len(field_names)`` → wrapped in
  :class:`BiasModel`, the natural reading of "one latent offset per field";
* takes only ``X`` and ``n_latent == 0`` → wrapped with an empty latent state;
* anything else → :class:`TwinModelError`, because guessing would hide a modelling bug.

classes.doc:
One Metrica sample match in metres (origin at the centre spot, x along the long side).

``players[team]`` is ``(T, n, 2)`` with NaN when a player is off the pitch; ``ball`` is ``(T, 2)``;
``events`` is the event table (pandas) with positions converted to metres.

children.doc:
Pass outcome: physics-based pitch control against data-only classifiers at equal data.

Train on one Metrica match, test on the other (and the swap). Every model sees the same passes:

* ``pc_default`` -- Spearman (2018) pitch control with the parameters common in open implementations (no fit);
* ``pc_reaction`` / ``pc_accel`` -- the same with the reaction-time or the acceleration-limited time to intercept,
  parameters fitted by maximum likelihood on the training passes (5 numbers);
* ``logistic`` / ``gbm`` -- logistic regression and gradient-boosted trees on geometric features
  (:func:`pitch_control.geometric_features`), no physics;
* ``hybrid`` -- the trees with the pitch-control probability and the intercept-time margin as extra features.

:func:`data_efficiency` repeats the comparison with 25 to all training passes (random subsets, several seeds).

functions.doc:
Probability that the attacking team controls the ball at ``target`` (vectorised over events).

Positions/velocities ``(n, players, 2)`` (NaN rows = absent players), ``ball_pos`` and ``target`` ``(n, 2)``;
``att_gk``/``def_gk`` are boolean masks ``(n, players)`` of goalkeepers. Returns ``(n,)``.

children.doc:
The ENSO study data set: monthly indices and maps built from the cached sources of :mod:`.data`.

:func:`build_dataset` returns an :class:`EnsoDataset` with, from ``start`` to ``end``:

* Nino 3.4 / 3 / 4 / 1+2 SST anomalies [K] from OISST v2.1 (box means of 1 deg monthly means);
* SST anomaly maps on the intermediate model's grid (default 2 deg x 1 deg, 120E-80W, 20S-20N);
* D20 anomalies [m] in 10 deg longitude bins (130E-80W) for 5S-5N and 2S-2N, gaps filled month by month from the
  available bins with the leading EOFs of the base period (:func:`eof_fill`; no month uses another month's data);
  the warm-water-volume proxy ``wwv`` is their zonal mean over 5S-5N, ``h_west`` / ``h_east`` the means west / east
  of 155W (the tilt mode);
* ERA5 zonal wind stress anomalies on the model grid and a Tahiti - Darwin pressure index (1959-2022 only; NaN
  after 2022-12).

All anomalies are taken from calendar-month climatologies of the ``base`` period -- choose it inside the
development period so the test period does not inform them. ``checks`` holds the cross-checks against independent
sources (statsmodels Nino 1+2, NCEI heat content, ERA5 SST).

functions.doc:
For each record of :func:`~.pipeline.memorise_vs_learn`: truth and the two variants' forecasts over the
end of the training period (left) and the start of the untouched test period (right). One shared legend;
each panel title carries the variants' RMSE on the whole training or test set.
